1
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:52,960
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,740
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:03,470
Dong.

4
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:08,020
Well, is my room a place
anyone can just walk into?

5
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:10,820
What's up?

6
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:12,760
Um, Ms. Wan said

7
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,760
the thing you instructed
won't work indoors.

8
00:01:15,039 --> 00:01:15,980
At 8:00 tonight,

9
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:17,420
she wants you to wait for her
at Yuhong Square.

10
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:18,420
Got it.

11
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:25,830
Ms. Wan.

12
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:28,070
It's freezing cold.

13
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:30,700
Do we have to do this at night?

14
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,750
Zhao Changyou died at 9:00 p.m.

15
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:35,990
We can only wait until this hour

16
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,990
to summon him back.

17
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,590
What do you mean?

18
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:42,810
We have to summon him back?

19
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:46,060
You guys

20
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,090
spent so long

21
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,289
looking for something here.

22
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:49,979
Did you find it?

23
00:01:50,330 --> 00:01:51,410
No, we didn't.

24
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,560
Come, take a look.

25
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:56,410
What is this?

26
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,780
-Take a look.
-Isn't this our stadium?

27
00:01:58,780 --> 00:01:59,630
What else could this be?

28
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:00,760
Wrong.

29
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,340
This is an incense burner.

30
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,200
Over there,

31
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,620
it's the altar.

32
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,740
If you want to find something,

33
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,410
it has to be done here.

34
00:02:55,079 --> 00:02:56,780
Aren't I dead?

35
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,250
How did I come back?

36
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:02,250
Changyou.

37
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:03,520
It's me.

38
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:05,030
It's me, Dong.

39
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,960
I can't see you.

40
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,380
I'm here. I'm here, Changyou.

41
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:09,800
I'm Dong.

42
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,780
Before you died,

43
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:12,430
didn't I order a batch of goods from you?

44
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:13,210
I even paid the deposit.

45
00:03:13,210 --> 00:03:14,310
Do you remember it?

46
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:18,630
I think so.

47
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,020
Death wipes the slate clean.

48
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,150
I can't return you the goods.

49
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,180
Later,

50
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:29,290
when you come down to me,

51
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,190
you can ask for it then.

52
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,530
If there's nothing else,

53
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:35,670
I'll be...

54
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:38,140
Changyou. Changyou. Changyou!

55
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:39,960
Changyou, don't go.

56
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,360
Where is the warehouse?

57
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,090
It's freezing cold.

58
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:43,520
Where am I supposed to find it, Changyou?

59
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:49,810
Did he come?

60
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,160
What did you two talk about?

61
00:03:51,710 --> 00:03:53,120
What's wrong with you?

62
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,190
I was asking about the key.

63
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:55,180
Why did you come back?

64
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:56,030
Hurry up!

65
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,630
Well, you should hurry up and ask him.

66
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:59,410
I'm so exhausted.

67
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:00,680
Hurry. Give me...

68
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,060
Give me my cane. Come on.

69
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,590
You really...

70
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,520
Hurry up!

71
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,110
Again.

72
00:04:31,190 --> 00:04:34,310
Follow the direction of my soybeans.

73
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:37,310
When all the scattered soybeans are found,

74
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,240
the key will appear.

75
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,659
Over there!

76
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:44,290
And there!

77
00:04:45,070 --> 00:04:47,800
That way.

78
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:50,060
Over here.

79
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:51,590
Over here.

80
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:53,740
Over here. Here. Here.

81
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,190
Over here. Over here.

82
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,990
Over here. Over here.

83
00:04:57,930 --> 00:04:59,659
Over here.

84
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:02,860
Over here.

85
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,730
Are you trying to fool me?

86
00:05:21,510 --> 00:05:22,240
Zhao Changyou?

87
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:24,950
Ms. Wan?

88
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,160
Are you okay?

89
00:05:27,450 --> 00:05:28,130
Ms. Wan.

90
00:05:38,159 --> 00:05:40,320
Zhao Changyou just left like that?

91
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:42,580
Just now, what came

92
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:44,690
wasn't only Zhao Changyou.

93
00:05:46,159 --> 00:05:47,070
What?

94
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,740
From this angle,

95
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,500
I just vaguely saw

96
00:05:53,010 --> 00:05:55,240
what happened that night.

97
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,770
Zhao Changyou

98
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,420
was sitting right there.

99
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,510
And there was

100
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,750
a young man next to him.

101
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,190
Who?

102
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:20,870
[Shasha Hair Salon]

103
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:39,800
Why do I like you so much?

104
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,330
I like you too, bro.

105
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:43,600
Sis.

106
00:06:44,130 --> 00:06:45,300
Cook me a bowl of noodles.

107
00:06:46,250 --> 00:06:47,340
You're so funny, bro.

108
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,860
Ordering food in a hair salon?

109
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:50,980
Well.

110
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:52,270
Alright.

111
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:54,130
I'll go to the restaurant
across the street for a bite.

112
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:54,890
Are you coming with me?

113
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:56,130
I'm not going.

114
00:06:56,159 --> 00:06:57,390
I don't want to eat at this hour.

115
00:06:58,770 --> 00:06:59,810
I'm really impressed.

116
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:00,890
I'm starving to death,

117
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,320
but you're not hungry at all.

118
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:12,660
1,500 yuan.

119
00:07:13,890 --> 00:07:15,010
Just for your skills,

120
00:07:15,010 --> 00:07:16,450
I must book you for a month.

121
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,920
That shows my heart.

122
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,300
I'm off.

123
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:21,630
Take care, bro.

124
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:22,180
Okay.

125
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:23,510
Wait for me.

126
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:48,250
[Yuhong Stadium]

127
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:53,870
Come in quickly.

128
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:55,390
Don't get stuck.

129
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:01,190
It's so early in the morning. You two...

130
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,530
What's wrong with your face?

131
00:10:04,530 --> 00:10:05,750
Why is it so swollen?

132
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,940
I-I got a toothache from an inflammation.

133
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,630
How serious is the inflammation?

134
00:10:14,370 --> 00:10:15,270
What happened?

135
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,010
Didn't you see?

136
00:10:17,010 --> 00:10:18,360
Another one froze at the stadium.

137
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:20,200
Be good and draw at Aunt Wan's.

138
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,390
Don't run around, okay?

139
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:24,150
What... What did I tell you?

140
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,700
The second one.

141
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:27,980
It's the second one already.

142
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:29,890
Stop talking nonsense.

143
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:30,740
Listen.

144
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:32,430
What's deadly now is not Yellow Immortal.

145
00:10:32,430 --> 00:10:33,010
What is it?

146
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,030
It's soybeans.

147
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:35,670
What soybeans?

148
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:38,200
A man stepped on soybeans.

149
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,710
Then he fell
and smashed his head on the stairs.

150
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:41,670
And he died.

151
00:10:42,770 --> 00:10:44,580
Who would be so wicked?

152
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,130
Feeding pigeons in the square in winter.

153
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:46,940
Was he really that bored?

154
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:47,820
Exactly.

155
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:50,000
He must have been very bored.

156
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,820
This door of yours—

157
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:51,850
don't open it. Do you hear me?

158
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:52,740
Don't go anywhere.

159
00:10:53,390 --> 00:10:54,530
I'll seal it.

160
00:10:54,530 --> 00:10:55,460
Don't worry.

161
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,360
What kind of person is that?

162
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:01,240
So bored.

163
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:06,790
Why scatter soybeans to feed pigeons?

164
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:07,790
You really...

165
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,340
Keep drawing.

166
00:11:15,820 --> 00:11:17,200
This sweetheart.

167
00:11:33,130 --> 00:11:35,080
Sweetheart, you keep drawing.

168
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:48,200
He really died from the fall?

169
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:50,550
How come this hand is missing?

170
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,670
Are you sure his hand was chopped off

171
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,080
after he died?

172
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,200
There's no splatter of blood.

173
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:58,320
And

174
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,650
the only fatal wound on his body

175
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,740
is on the back of his head.

176
00:12:01,370 --> 00:12:02,150
On the steps,

177
00:12:02,150 --> 00:12:03,120
there are crushed soybeans.

178
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,240
And the traces

179
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,130
match the path of his movement.

180
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,440
Could it be

181
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,630
that someone pushed him to the ground
and killed him,

182
00:12:10,130 --> 00:12:11,390
and then chopped off his hand?

183
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:13,320
If there had been a struggle,

184
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,550
there would definitely be traces
at the scene.

185
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:15,820
But from what we can see now,

186
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:16,740
I don't think the body has been moved.

187
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,360
What about other people's footprints?

188
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:19,740
Oh man, there are so many.

189
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,880
Look... Look at all these people.

190
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,290
When we received the report

191
00:12:21,550 --> 00:12:22,760
[Paintwork] [Waxing] [Polishing]

192
00:12:22,290 --> 00:12:23,480
and arrived at the scene,

193
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:25,650
we'd already seen a few different crowds
come and go.

194
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,580
Any useful footprints
were destroyed long ago.

195
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:29,100
Everyone's trampled all over them.

196
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:30,100
In other words,

197
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,980
it's possible that yesterday,
it was an accidental death.

198
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:34,100
Later, someone saw the body

199
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,200
and chopped off the hand.

200
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,000
Who are you?

201
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:38,460
He Liang,

202
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,870
from the Yingjin
Municipal Criminal Investigation Unit.

203
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:40,940
He's here to work on a case.

204
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:42,550
Hello.

205
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,170
Theoretically,

206
00:12:44,170 --> 00:12:45,290
we can't rule out that possibility.

207
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:46,580
But

208
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:47,600
for the final results,

209
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,550
we still have to wait
for the autopsy report.

210
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,510
Tell me,

211
00:12:53,890 --> 00:12:55,270
the person who chopped off the hand—

212
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:56,700
what was he after?

213
00:12:57,670 --> 00:12:59,910
In criminal psychology,
there's something called necrophilia.

214
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,250
They don't like killing people.

215
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:03,770
They're just interested in corpses.

216
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:04,910
I know.

217
00:13:04,910 --> 00:13:06,720
Some weird foreign fetish.

218
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:07,790
They even dig up people's graves.

219
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:08,820
But around here,

220
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,220
I've never heard of anything like that.

221
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,750
Tomb raiding
is just about stealing things.

222
00:13:16,130 --> 00:13:17,940
What are they asking about
at the hair salon?

223
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:20,050
Wang Ping.

224
00:13:20,270 --> 00:13:21,410
She said she was the last one

225
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,550
to see Li Dewu.

226
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:24,330
After Li Dewu left here,

227
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,500
he said he was hungry
and wanted a bowl of noodles.

228
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:28,450
There's a noodle shop nearby?

229
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,480
Um, yes. You can go this way.
There's a shortcut.

230
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:34,050
It's in this direction.

231
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:09,130
Where have you been
for the past half a year?

232
00:14:09,130 --> 00:14:10,290
You didn't even call me.

233
00:14:13,050 --> 00:14:13,700
Sister.

234
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:15,130
Where do you live?

235
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:16,690
You came back but didn't come home!

236
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,550
I... I just got back.

237
00:14:19,550 --> 00:14:20,700
Just a couple of days ago.

238
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,940
I went h-home and knocked,
but there was no answer.

239
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,240
I thought you were on a business trip.

240
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:26,480
So I stayed at a former classmate's place
for a couple of days.

241
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:29,650
Um...

242
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:32,010
this is my younger brother, Liu Yang.

243
00:14:32,650 --> 00:14:33,450
This is He Liang,

244
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,290
a comrade from Yingjin.

245
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,410
He's here on a business trip.

246
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,600
He'll stay in your room for a few days.

247
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,580
Oh man, it's going to be lively.

248
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,940
Four people live in one house.

249
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:41,720
Four?

250
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,890
It's a long story.

251
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:45,960
Let's go.

252
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:46,890
My brother-in-law is back?

253
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,100
What are you talking about?

254
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,290
Stop talking nonsense.

255
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:50,360
Look at the dirt on your back.

256
00:15:02,790 --> 00:15:04,320
I'll hurry up and clean up

257
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,860
that room for you.

258
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:19,840
No need, Sister.

259
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,620
I'll just stay at San Yan'er's place.

260
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:23,290
You have your own home.

261
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:24,370
Why go stay at someone else's place?

262
00:15:24,370 --> 00:15:25,460
People will laugh at us.

263
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:36,630
Didn't you take his money?

264
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:39,000
He's out working on his case
during the day.

265
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,120
He only comes back at night

266
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,360
to get some sleep.

267
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:43,460
You two probably
won't even see each other.

268
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,150
If he's not happy,

269
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:46,700
he can go stay at a hostel.

270
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:48,240
I'll just charge him for meals.

271
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:51,290
Isn't that fine?

272
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:55,440
You... You're not short
of this little money, are you?

273
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,650
Of course I'm short of money.

274
00:15:58,670 --> 00:15:59,620
Don't let her small size fool you.

275
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:00,670
She can eat a lot in a day.

276
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:01,820
She always wants snacks,

277
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:02,630
asking me to buy them for her.

278
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,890
Why aren't you taking off your coat?

279
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:05,940
What are you standing here for?

280
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,550
I said I'd support you after graduation.

281
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,960
But these past few years,
I haven't saved much money.

282
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,370
Why are you saying that?

283
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:21,960
Isn't it great that you're back?

284
00:16:25,370 --> 00:16:27,480
When I heard your forest farm caught fire,

285
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,440
I couldn't sleep for nights.

286
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:31,750
I kept telling Mom and Dad every day

287
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
that if they saw you,

288
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,120
don't talk to you

289
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,740
and just kick you back here.

290
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,860
Aren't you a cop? And you believe in that?

291
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:42,460
When you called me,

292
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:43,580
I was stunned.

293
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,370
I wondered,

294
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,630
with such a big fire,

295
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,050
how did you escape?

296
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:49,290
They kicked me back.

297
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:51,080
You're never serious.

298
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,290
Sit. Sit for a while. Sit.

299
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:54,500
You must be exhausted.

300
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:07,609
If I talk to her,

301
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,609
can she understand?

302
00:17:08,609 --> 00:17:09,790
Yes, go ahead.

303
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:15,460
Do you want to eat fried pork?

304
00:17:15,849 --> 00:17:17,960
I want to eat chicken drumsticks.

305
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,310
What did she say? I don't understand.

306
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:21,250
She's just like you,

307
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:22,720
as greedy as you were
when you were little.

308
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,250
She loves things with strong flavors.

309
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:26,290
She said she wants to eat chicken butt.

310
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,570
She likes eating chicken butt?

311
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,130
Who eats that stuff?

312
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:34,010
She likes it.

313
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,070
Didn't she just pound her legs?

314
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:39,740
Are you... Are you hungry?

315
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,180
I'm... I'm okay.

316
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:42,850
I'll make you something good.

317
00:17:46,290 --> 00:17:47,550
I'll do it. I'll do it.

318
00:17:47,550 --> 00:17:49,180
How about some fried steamed bun slices?

319
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:49,810
Fried steamed bun slices?

320
00:17:49,810 --> 00:17:50,860
Fried steamed bun slices are good.

321
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:53,350
Spread some fermented bean curd on them.

322
00:17:53,350 --> 00:17:54,270
Yes, yes, yes.

323
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,030
I'll make some soup.

324
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,050
Great.
